[Event "Bowdler Attack setup"]
[ChapterName "Bowdler Attack setup"]
[Annotator "Notes: Opening Night, on Nathaniel Tucker's setup"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 { The Bowdler Attack: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp. } 2... e6 { Black blunts the bishop and gets ready to chase it with ...d5. } 3. a3 { Makes room for the bishop on a2, where ...d5 and ...b5 can't win time against it. } 3... a6 4. Ba2 { From a2 the bishop keeps its aim at f7 and e6, out of reach. } 4... Nc6 5. d3 { A solid centre: e4 stays protected, so the knights are free to go to e2 and c3. } 5... g6 6. Ne2 { The knight goes to e2 rather than f3, so the f-pawn can still push to f4. } 6... Bg7 7. O-O Nge7 8. Nbc3 O-O 9. Ng3 { The knight heads for the kingside, ready to back up f4 and f5 and to jump to h5. } 9... b6 10. Bg5 Qc7 11. f4 { The plan: push f4 and f5 to open the f-file against Black's king, with the a2 bishop aiming down at f7. } *
